# The real GlobalPlatform flow, end to end.
#
#   terminal -> ISD (card manager) -> loader -> JCRE -> JVM -> applet
#
# Run with:  ./run.sh gpflow.jcvm

genwallet wallet.cap

# 1. Select the card manager. No applet exists yet, so this is the only
#    thing on the card that can answer.
send 00 A4 04 00 00

# 2. Open a secure channel. No SCP keys here, so these are accepted
#    without verification, but the sequence is the real one.
send 80 50 00 00 08 0102030405060708
send 84 82 00 00 10 00112233445566778899AABBCCDDEEFF

# 3. INSTALL [for load]: tell the card an ELF with this AID is coming.
#    Then LOAD blocks carry the CAP components, then INSTALL [for install
#    and make selectable] runs the applet's install() and registers it.
#    gpload builds and sends exactly that sequence.
# 'load' and 'install' now build and send these APDUs themselves, so the
# short commands and the raw sequence are the same path.
load wallet.cap
install A0000001020304

# 4. What is on the card now.
gp
send 80 F2 40 00 02 4F00

# 5. Select the applet and use it. From here the card manager is out of
#    the picture; APDUs go straight to Applet.process.
send 00 A4 04 00 07 A0000001020304
send B0 50 00 00 02
send B0 30 00 00 02 00 64
send B0 50 00 00 02

# 6. Delete it again.
send 00 A4 04 00 00
send 80 E4 00 80 09 4F 07 A0000001020304
gp
quit
